<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the scalability and portability, the low-altitude intelligent networks (LAINs)
are essential in various fields such as surveillance and disaster rescue.
However, in LAINs, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are characterized by
the distributed topology and high dynamic mobility, and vulnerable to security threats,
which may degrade the routing performance for data transmission.
Hence, how to ensure the routing stability and security of LAINs is a challenge.
In this paper, we focus on the routing process in LAINs with multiple UAV clusters
and propose the blockchain-enabled zero-trust architecture to manage the joining and exiting of UAVs.
Furthermore, we formulate the routing problem to minimize the end-to-end (E2E)
delay, which is an integer linear programming and intractable to solve.
Therefore, considering the distribution of LAINs,
we reformulate the routing problem into a decentralized partially observable Markov decision process.
With the proposed soft hierarchical experience replay buffer,
the multi-agent double deep Q-network based adaptive routing algorithm is designed.
Finally, simulations are conducted and numerical results show that the total
E2E delay of the proposed mechanism decreases by 22.38% than the benchmark on average.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Low-altitude intelligent networks, trusted routing, blockchain, soft hierarchical experience replay buffer,
multi-agent deep reinforcement learning.

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>s key components of the six generation communication networks,
the low-altitude intelligent network (LAINs) are widely applied to multiple tasks,
such as disaster rescue and real-time monitoring <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.
In these applications, the data generated from sensor devices (SDs) are required to be
relayed to the remote ground base stations (BSs) by unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
Particularly, UAVs act as aerial relays and cooperatively accomplish the data collection
and transmission, providing low-cost, flexible, and versatile services.
In LAINs, routing is a significant issue for data transmission <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, since UAVs in LAINs are characterized by the complex application
environment, high mobility and distributed topology, they are vulnerable
to security threats and unreliable, i.e., attacks and node failures.
Thus, the availability of communication links is susceptible,
which leads to the reduction of routing performances.
Hence, it is significant to efficiently manage the mobility of UAVs in the zero-trust environment.
There exist a couple of works related to the management of UAVs.
For instance, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, the ground control station (GCS) is responsible
for managing the connection among all UAVs, through the status message sent by UAVs.
In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, the authors present that as the center controller and manager,
the GCS receives the data transmitted by UAVs, which is suffered from long distances,
undulating terrains or other interferences.
Authors in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> present that the GCS remotely controls UAVs by sending controlling information,
in which the relay UAV is limited within the communication range of the GCS,
restricting the scope of operations.
Moreover, the above works rely on a center controller, which is not resilient
to fault tolerance and may be susceptible to tampering.
Hence, how to guarantee the reliability and security of routing remains challenging
in the distributed and zero-trust network.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Meanwhile, the transmission delay is a key quality of service,
since low delay can significantly improve the timeliness and reliability for
various emergency applications, such as the surveillance information transmission <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.
Therefore, it is necessary to design an adaptive and
dynamic algorithm to enable timely and reliable routing
in the varying network topology.
To tackle this issue, the multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) can be applied <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.
Specifically, there exist a couple of works focusing on MARL-based routing problems in dynamic scenarios.
For example, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, the authors propose a value decomposition network based MARL algorithm to
minimize the end-to-end (E2E) delay of packet routing within dynamic aerial and terrestrial hybrid networks.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> formulates the packet routing as a max-min problem using the Lagrange method,
and proposes a constrained MARL dynamic routing algorithm to balance the objective improvement and constraint satisfaction.
Authors in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> establish the mean-field enhanced heterogeneous MARL framework
to optimize the communication energy efficiency during routing.
The above studys illustrate that the MARL can solve the routing problem effectively.
However, these works do not consider the mobility management of UAVs in the zero-trust environment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To deal with the above challenges, in this paper, the routing process is depicted
in the zero-trust LAINs with multiple UAV clusters, considering the dynamic joining and exiting of UAVs.
Meanwhile, to improve the network reliability and security, the blockchain technique with a distributed ledger is
introduced to manage the mobility of nodes and avoid being tempered with, by leveraging the smart contract.
Further, a couple of UAVs with powerful capabilities are selected to construct the decentralized controller in the blockchain.
In light of the constructed LAIN,
the routing problem is formulated to minimize the total E2E delay,
which is an integer linear programming (ILP) and intractable to solve.
Besides, it is tricky to obtain the global information due to decentralized UAVs.
Hence, we reformulate the routing problem into a decentralized partially observable Markov decision process (Dec-POMDP).
To improve the efficiency of learning and training,
we propose the multi-agent double deep Q-network (MADDQN)-based adaptive routing approach
with the designed soft hierarchical experience replay buffer (SHERB).
Finally, numerical simulations are conducted to verify the performance of the proposed algorithm.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">System Model and Problem Formulation</span></h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Network Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The routing process in zero-trust LAINs is show in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A Network Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
including <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> nodes, and each node holds a unique identity.
Specifically, when there exist UAVs applying to joining or exiting,
the identities are authenticated and managed by smart contracts via the blockchain technique.
Moreover, the periodical authentication is performed on all UAVs for the persistent verification.
In detail, the ground layer consists of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> BSs and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> SDs.
The air layer is composed of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> UAVs.
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\!=\!\{1,...,b,...,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\!=\!\{1,...,b,...,B\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}\!=\!\{1,...,i,...,I\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}\!=\!\{1,...,i,...,I\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}\!=\!\{1,...,u,...,U\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}\!=\!\{1,...,u,...,U\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sets of
BSs, SDs, and UAVs, respectively.
Besides, UAV set <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚍</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is divided based on clusters, in which <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the data collection, relay forwarding, and downlinking clusters, respectively.
In each cluster, the UAV with the most energy and computing power is selected as the cluster head.
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\!=\!\mathcal{E}_{iu}\!+\!\mathcal{E}_{uu}\!+\!\mathcal{E}_{ub}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\!=\!\mathcal{E}_{iu}\!+\!\mathcal{E}_{uu}\!+\!\mathcal{E}_{ub}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the set of communication
link status among all nodes, where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{iu}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{iu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{iu}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{iu}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{ub}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{ub}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{ub}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{ub}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{uu}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{uu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{uu}\!\in\!\mathcal{E}_{uu}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the connection of links
between the SD and UAV, the BS and UAV, and the UAV and UAV, respectively.
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{nm}\in\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{nm}\in\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether there exists a communicable link
between nodes <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{nm}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{nm}=1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the link is effective,
and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{nm}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{nm}=0</annotation></semantics></math> denotes there exist no direct links.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, the time period is divided into <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}</annotation></semantics></math> steps.
The set of time steps is represented as <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!=\!\{1,...,t,...,\mathsf{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!=\!\{1,...,t,...,\mathsf{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
At the beginning of time step <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, demand <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is transmitted from SD <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to
destination BS <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varUpsilon^{r}\!=\!\{\mathtt{s}^{r},\mathcal{L}^{r},\mathtt{d}^{r},\mathcal{T}^{r}_{max}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚍</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varUpsilon^{r}\!=\!\{\mathtt{s}^{r},\mathcal{L}^{r},\mathtt{d}^{r},\mathcal{T}^{r}_{max}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
in which the source is <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{s}^{r}\!=\!i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{s}^{r}\!=\!i</annotation></semantics></math>, and the destination is <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{d}^{r}\!=\!b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚍</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{d}^{r}\!=\!b</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, the size of demand <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> (in bit),
and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{r}_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{r}_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum delay tolerance of the demand transmission.
Further, demands are uploaded from SD <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\!\in\!\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\!\in\!\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
relayed by UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and downloaded
from UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> to BS <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\!\in\!\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\!\in\!\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{ib}^{r}\!=\!{(e_{iu},\cdots,e_{ub})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{ib}^{r}\!=\!{(e_{iu},\cdots,e_{ub})}</annotation></semantics></math>
indicates a completed routing path for transmitting demand <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The coordinates of SD <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>
and BS <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> remain fixed and are <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varTheta}_{i}\!=\!{(x_{i},y_{i},0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varTheta}_{i}\!=\!{(x_{i},y_{i},0)}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varTheta}_{b}\!=\!{(x_{b},y_{b},0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varTheta}_{b}\!=\!{(x_{b},y_{b},0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The location of UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is indicated by
<math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varTheta}_{u}(t)={(x_{u}(t),y_{u}(t),z_{u}(t))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varTheta}_{u}(t)={(x_{u}(t),y_{u}(t),z_{u}(t))}</annotation></semantics></math> in three-dimensional Cartesian coordinates at time step <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Additionally, the Euclidean distance between nodes <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>
is indicated by <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{nm}(t)\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{nm}(t)\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{(x_{n}(t)\!-\!x_{m}(t))^{2}\!+\!(y_{n}(t)\!-\!y_{m}(t))^{2}\!+\!(z_{n}(t)\!-\!z_{m}(t))^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{(x_{n}(t)\!-\!x_{m}(t))^{2}\!+\!(y_{n}(t)\!-\!y_{m}(t))^{2}\!+\!(z_{n}(t)\!-\!z_{m}(t))^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, the distance between UAVs should satisfy</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}d_{min}\leqslant d_{nm}(t),\forall n,m\in\mathcal{U},n\neq m,t\in T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}d_{min}\leqslant d_{nm}(t),\forall n,m\in\mathcal{U},n\neq m,t\in T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{min}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the safe distance to avoid collisions among UAVs.
At time step <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of connected UAVs for UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and distance <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u\kappa}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u\kappa}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> between UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}d_{u\kappa}(t)\leqslant d_{u,max},\forall\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U},t\in T," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}d_{u\kappa}(t)\leqslant d_{u,max},\forall\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U},t\in T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">in which <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u,max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u,max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum communication distance of UAV <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.22745v1/Scenario.4.20.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/214;" width="429" height="214" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span> Routing scenario in zero-trust LAINs with the mobility management of UAVs via the blockchain technique.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Blockchain Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To manage the mobility of UAVs, a lightweight blockchain model is proposed.
Additionally, to maintain the sustainability and reliability of routing,
the joining and exiting of UAVs need to be recorded and updated via the blockchain.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>1 </span>Role Selection</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the lightweight blockchain, the set <math id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> of UAVs is divided into the sets of full nodes
<math id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{f}=\{1,2,\cdots,u_{f}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{f}=\{1,2,\cdots,u_{f}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and light nodes <math id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{l}=\{1,2,\cdots,u_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{l}=\{1,2,\cdots,u_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In detail, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A Network Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
cluster head UAVs are selected as full nodes due to the sufficient resources,
while the other UAVs act as light nodes in LAINs.
In particular, the full nodes have the full blockchain ledger and are responsible for the blockchain consensus,
including broadcasting and verification of transactions.
The light nodes can only store the header of blocks and are in charge of generating local transactions and relaying transactions from other UAVs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>2 </span>PBFT-based Consensus Process</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We apply the practical Byzantine fault tolerance (PBFT) method,
which can ensure the success of the consensus process when the number of failure nodes is less than one third.
For the effectiveness and reliability of the PBFT consensus,
it is significant to select consensus UAVs with the most abundant resources as the primary node,
while other consensus UAVs operate as non-primary (replica) nodes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>3 </span>Transaction Generation and Broadcasting</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transactions waiting for the consensus are generated periodically and include the status of UAVs,
i.e., the queue buffer, location, and information of neighboring nodes.
Then, all generated transactions are broadcasted to the entire network via the Gossip protocol for verifying.
After verification, the transactions are added to the transaction pool of the blockchain and then synchronized to the
entire blockchain. Once a consensus is reached, the data transaction are recorded in the blockchain with tamper-proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span> </span><span id="S2.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Delay Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A Network Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, in LAINs, the E2E routing delay consists of the total
transmission delay on the multi-hop path from the source UAV to destination UAV.
Since the delay is constrained by data transmission rate <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, it is essential to
analyze the channel characteristics of both ground-to-air and air-to-air wireless communication links.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Regard to demand <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, binary variable <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!\in\!\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!\in\!\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> clarifies
the transmission status, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!=\!\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;1,\!\text{ if }\!r\!\text{ is on node }n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}\text{ at time step }\!t,\\
&amp;0,\!\text{ otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.772em;" width="0.772em"><mtext> if </mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.309em;" width="0.309em"><mi>r</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is on node </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:4.568em;" width="4.568em"><mtext> at time step </mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mtext> otherwise</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!=\!\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;1,\!\text{ if }\!r\!\text{ is on node }n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}\text{ at time step }\!t,\\
&amp;0,\!\text{ otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Besides, binary variable <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{nm}^{r}(t)\!\in\!\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{nm}^{r}(t)\!\in\!\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes whether demand <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>
passes link <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{nm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{nm}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>), i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}\eta_{nm}^{r}(t)\!=\!\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;1,\!\text{ if }\!r\!\text{ is transmitted via }\!e_{nm}\!\text{ at time step }\!t,\\
&amp;0,\!\text{ otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.772em;" width="0.772em"><mtext> if </mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.309em;" width="0.309em"><mi>r</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:7.405em;" width="7.405em"><mtext> is transmitted via </mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:4.568em;" width="4.568em"><mtext> at time step </mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mtext> otherwise</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}\eta_{nm}^{r}(t)\!=\!\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;1,\!\text{ if }\!r\!\text{ is transmitted via }\!e_{nm}\!\text{ at time step }\!t,\\
&amp;0,\!\text{ otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Further, <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the path loss between nodes <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>
and remains constant within time step <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{nm}(t)=20\log\left(\frac{4\pi\lambda}{c}d_{nm}(t)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{nm}(t)=20\log\left(\frac{4\pi\lambda}{c}d_{nm}(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\omega\left[{\Pr}_{nm}(t)\left(\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}(t)-\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)\right)+\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>LoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>NLoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>NLoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\omega\left[{\Pr}_{nm}(t)\left(\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}(t)-\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)\right)+\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>LoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>NLoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{NLoS}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
represent the additional path losses under LoS and non-LoS (NLoS) propagations, respectively.
When <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the path loss from <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
While <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the path loss between UAVs.
<math id="S2.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> represents the carrier frequency, and <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the speed of light.
Besides, <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Pr}_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Pr}_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the probability that there exist line of sight (LoS) links between SDs/BSs and UAVs, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}{\Pr}_{nm}(t)\!=\!\frac{1}{1\!+\!\varrho_{1}\!\exp\left\{\!-\!\varrho_{2}\!\left[\!\frac{180}{\pi}\!\arctan\!\left(\!\frac{h_{nm}(t)}{xy_{nm}(t)}\!\right)\!-\!\varrho_{1}\!\right]\!\right\}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>180</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.760em;" width="2.760em"><mi>arctan</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo>]</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}{\Pr}_{nm}(t)\!=\!\frac{1}{1\!+\!\varrho_{1}\!\exp\left\{\!-\!\varrho_{2}\!\left[\!\frac{180}{\pi}\!\arctan\!\left(\!\frac{h_{nm}(t)}{xy_{nm}(t)}\!\right)\!-\!\varrho_{1}\!\right]\!\right\}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">in which <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varrho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varrho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varrho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varrho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the constant parameters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since LAINs are characterized by high mobility and unstable data traffic fluctuations,
we introduce a queue buffer for each node <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> to alleviate the network congestion.
In particular, for node <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the amount of demands received at time step <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\!-\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\!-\!1</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
At time step <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the queued demand set, queue length, maximum queue capacity,
and the number of transmitted demands of node <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> are denoted as
<math id="S2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)=\{r,\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!=\!1,\forall r\!\in\!R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)=\{r,\zeta_{n}^{r}(t)\!=\!1,\forall r\!\in\!R\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}^{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}^{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In detail,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{}\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)\!=\!\sum_{r\in R}\sum_{{m}\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}}\eta^{r}_{{m}n}(t\!-\!1),0\!\leq\!\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)\!\leq\!C_{n}^{max},\\
&amp;C_{n}(t)=\sum_{r\in R}\zeta_{n}^{r}(t),0\leq C_{n}(t)\!\leq\!C_{n}^{max},C_{n}(t)\!=\!\left\lvert\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)\right\rvert,\\
&amp;\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)\!=\!\sum_{r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)}\sum_{{m}\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}}\eta^{r}_{n{m}}(t),\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)\!=\!C_{n}(t).\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>|</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{}\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)\!=\!\sum_{r\in R}\sum_{{m}\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}}\eta^{r}_{{m}n}(t\!-\!1),0\!\leq\!\varepsilon_{n}^{re}(t\!-\!1)\!\leq\!C_{n}^{max},\\
&amp;C_{n}(t)=\sum_{r\in R}\zeta_{n}^{r}(t),0\leq C_{n}(t)\!\leq\!C_{n}^{max},C_{n}(t)\!=\!\left\lvert\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)\right\rvert,\\
&amp;\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)\!=\!\sum_{r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)}\sum_{{m}\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}}\eta^{r}_{n{m}}(t),\varepsilon_{n}^{tr}(t)\!=\!C_{n}(t).\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here, the UAV leverages the parallel transmission for demands,
indicating that UAVs forward all demands received from the last time step.
Besides, the adaptive channel bandwidth allocation scheme is designed
to narrow the transmission delay gap of different demands in one time step.
Hence, at time step <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the allocated bandwidth <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{r}_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{r}_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated based on the size of demand <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}B^{r}_{n}(t)\!=\!\frac{\mathcal{L}^{r}}{\sum\limits_{k\in\mathcal{C}_{n}\!(t)}\!\mathcal{L}^{k}}B_{n}(t),\forall n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\!\cup\!\mathcal{U},r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{n}(t),t\!\in\!T," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}B^{r}_{n}(t)\!=\!\frac{\mathcal{L}^{r}}{\sum\limits_{k\in\mathcal{C}_{n}\!(t)}\!\mathcal{L}^{k}}B_{n}(t),\forall n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\!\cup\!\mathcal{U},r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{n}(t),t\!\in\!T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the total bandwidth of node <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Based on Shannon theory, at time step <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, transmission rate <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{r}_{nm}\!(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{r}_{nm}\!(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for demand <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> from nodes <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\!\cup\!\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\!\cup\!\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>
to <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\!\cup\!\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\!\cup\!\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}G_{nm}^{r}(t)\!=\!B^{r}_{n}(t)\log_{2}\!\left(\!1\!+\!\frac{P^{tr}_{nm}(t)\cdot 10^{\frac{-{L_{nm}(t)}}{10}}}{\sigma^{2}_{nm}(t)}\!\right)\!,r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}G_{nm}^{r}(t)\!=\!B^{r}_{n}(t)\log_{2}\!\left(\!1\!+\!\frac{P^{tr}_{nm}(t)\cdot 10^{\frac{-{L_{nm}(t)}}{10}}}{\sigma^{2}_{nm}(t)}\!\right)\!,r\in\mathcal{C}_{n}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{tr}_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{tr}_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{nm}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{nm}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
indicate the transmission power and noise power between nodes <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Then, the transmission delay for demands from nodes <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{nm}(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{nm}(t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{r\in R}\frac{\mathcal{L}^{r}}{G^{r}_{nm}(t)}\eta^{r}_{nm}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{r\in R}\frac{\mathcal{L}^{r}}{G^{r}_{nm}(t)}\eta^{r}_{nm}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall r\in R,n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B},t\in T." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall r\in R,n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B},t\in T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">When the routing path <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{r}_{ib}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{r}_{ib}</annotation></semantics></math> for transmitting demand <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>
from source SD <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to destination BS <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>
is determined, E2E delay <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> can
be calculated as</p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{r}\!=\!\underset{t\in T}{\sum}\underset{{e_{nm}\in\mathcal{P}_{ib}^{r}}}{\sum}\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{nm}(t),\forall r\!\in\!R,n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.0539em">=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.0539em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">e</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">b</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{r}\!=\!\underset{t\in T}{\sum}\underset{{e_{nm}\in\mathcal{P}_{ib}^{r}}}{\sum}\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{nm}(t),\forall r\!\in\!R,n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-D</span> </span><span id="S2.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Formulation</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The objective is to minimize the total E2E delay of LAINs with the mobility of nodes,
and the corresponding optimization problem is formulated as</p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{P}0:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{P}0:</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underset{{\bm{\eta,\zeta}}}{\textrm{min}}\;\mathcal{T}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝜼</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="bold">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝜻</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underset{{\bm{\eta,\zeta}}}{\textrm{min}}\;\mathcal{T}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textrm{s.t.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textrm{s.t.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(\ref{distance_min}), (\ref{distance_max}), (\ref{zeta-demands}), (\ref{eta-link}), (\ref{re_tr})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E2" title="In II-A Network Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext><mtext>), (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E3" title="In II-A Network Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext><mtext>), (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E4" title="In II-C Delay Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></mtext><mtext>), (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E5" title="In II-C Delay Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></mtext><mtext>), (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E8" title="In II-C Delay Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(\ref{distance_min}), (\ref{distance_max}), (\ref{zeta-demands}), (\ref{eta-link}), (\ref{re_tr})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E13Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}}\!\eta^{r}_{nm}(t)\!=\!1,\forall r\!\in\!R,t\!\in\!T,e_{nm}\!\in\mathcal{E}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}}\!\eta^{r}_{nm}(t)\!=\!1,\forall r\!\in\!R,t\!\in\!T,e_{nm}\!\in\mathcal{E},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E13Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\eta}=\{\eta_{nm}^{r}(t),\forall t\in T,e_{nm}\in\mathcal{E},n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B},r\in R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\eta}=\{\eta_{nm}^{r}(t),\forall t\in T,e_{nm}\in\mathcal{E},n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},m\in\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B},r\in R\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\zeta}=\{\zeta_{n}^{r}(t),\forall t\in T,n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},r\in R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\zeta}=\{\zeta_{n}^{r}(t),\forall t\in T,n\in\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U},r\in R\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Besides, the demand <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> from node <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\!\in\!\mathcal{I}\cup\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> can
only be received by one another node <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\cup\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is observed that <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}0</annotation></semantics></math> is in the form of ILP and
NP-hard to deal with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design</span></h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dec-POMDP based Reformulation</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since each UAV has a local observation rather than global observation,
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}0</annotation></semantics></math> is reformulated as a Dec-POMDP, to cater for the dynamically changing network environment.
Each UAV in LAINs is regarded as an independent agent and makes its own routing decision
that sends a demand to an alternative next UAV. Hence, the set of all agents is equal to UAV set <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.
At each time step <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> observes local state <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of the environment
and executes action <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> according to the observable state.
Then, agent <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> receives an immediate reward <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{u}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{u}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the environment is transfered to next observation state <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}({t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}({t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The tuple <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}(t),o_{u}({t+1}),f_{u}(t)\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}(t),o_{u}({t+1}),f_{u}(t)\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>
indicates the transition experience of agent <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and is explained in detail.</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">State space <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>: At time step <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the observable state <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of agent <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>
includes the available information of the current UAV and neighboring UAVs, detailed as</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{u}(t)\!=\!\{\Theta_{u}(t),\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\Theta_{\kappa}(t),\mathcal{C}_{\kappa}(t)\},\kappa\!\in\!\Gamma_{u}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{u}(t)\!=\!\{\Theta_{u}(t),\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\Theta_{\kappa}(t),\mathcal{C}_{\kappa}(t)\},\kappa\!\in\!\Gamma_{u}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Wherein, <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{k}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{k}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indicate the locations of UAV <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and neighbor UAV <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
<math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\kappa}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\kappa}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are the set of queued demands on UAVs <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The queued demand set includes the information tuple <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varUpsilon^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varUpsilon^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> of each demand <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
The observations of all agents are aggregated into joint state <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> in time step <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
denoted as <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}(t)=\{o_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}(t)=\{o_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the state space is indicated as <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{\bm{s}(t)|t\in T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{\bm{s}(t)|t\in T\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Action sapce <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>: Agent <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> makes decisions for each carried demand independently,
and the set <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}(t)=\{a_{u}^{r}(t),r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}(t)=\{a_{u}^{r}(t),r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the actions
for demand <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Wherein, each sub-action <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the next-hop neighboring node
selected by UAV <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to relay demand <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}a_{u}^{r}(t)\in\{\Gamma_{u}(t)\},u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}},\\
a_{u}^{r}(t)\in\{\Gamma_{u}(t),Z_{u}(t)\},u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚜</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚍</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}a_{u}^{r}(t)\in\{\Gamma_{u}(t)\},u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{s}}\cup\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{r}},\\
a_{u}^{r}(t)\in\{\Gamma_{u}(t),Z_{u}(t)\},u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of BSs connected with UAV <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the destination BS <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> of demand <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> connects to UAV <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>𝚍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}_{\mathtt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the demand is directly transmitted to destination <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> by UAV <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the contrary, the demand is relayed by neighboring UAVs.
The actions of all agents are aggregated as <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}(t)=\{a_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}(t)=\{a_{u}(t),u\in\mathcal{U}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in time step <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the action space is <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{\bm{a}(t)|t\in T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{\bm{a}(t)|t\in T\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reward <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{u}(t)\!=\!\{\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{u}(t)\!=\!\{\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the reward that agent <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> obtains after transmitting demand <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to neighboring node
<math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}\mathcal{R}^{r}_{u}(t)=\frac{1}{\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{u\kappa}(t)}\eta_{u\kappa}^{r}(t),\forall r\in\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}\mathcal{R}^{r}_{u}(t)=\frac{1}{\mathcal{T}^{tr,r}_{u\kappa}(t)}\eta_{u\kappa}^{r}(t),\forall r\in\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transition flag <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(t)\!=\!\{f^{r}(t)|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(t)\!=\!\{f^{r}(t)|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether demand <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> arrives at destination BS <math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\!\in\!\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\!\in\!\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{r}{(t)}\!=\!\begin{cases}\!1,\text{if }a_{u}^{r}{(t)}\text{ is the destination BS }b,\\
\!0,\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is the destination BS </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{r}{(t)}\!=\!\begin{cases}\!1,\text{if }a_{u}^{r}{(t)}\text{ is the destination BS }b,\\
\!0,\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discount factor <math id="S3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S3.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\gamma}=\{\gamma_{u}|u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜸</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\gamma}=\{\gamma_{u}|u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
in which <math id="S3.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is designed to calculate the cumulative reward.
A larger <math id="S3.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> indicates decisions focusing on the long-term reward.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The policy <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> leads agent <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to select action <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for demand <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>
under observation <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\pi}_{u}(t)=\{\pi_{u}^{r}(t),\forall r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi}_{u}(t)=\{\pi_{u}^{r}(t),\forall r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the joint policy of all demands on agent <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\Pi}(t)=\{\bm{\pi}_{u}(t),\forall u\in\mathcal{U}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Pi}(t)=\{\bm{\pi}_{u}(t),\forall u\in\mathcal{U}\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the policy of all agents.
According to the Dec-POMDP and specific policy <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Pi}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Pi}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can obtain the routing path for all demands.
Therefore, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}0</annotation></semantics></math> is transformed to find the optimal
policy <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\Pi}^{\star}(t)=\{\bm{\pi}_{u}^{\star}(t),\forall u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Pi}^{\star}(t)=\{\bm{\pi}_{u}^{\star}(t),\forall u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and then the improved MADRL-based routing method is designed to
obtain <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Pi}^{\star}=\{\bm{\Pi}^{\star}(t)|t\in T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Pi}^{\star}=\{\bm{\Pi}^{\star}(t)|t\in T\}</annotation></semantics></math> for minimizing the total E2E delay.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In dynamic scenarios with multiple sources and destinations,
to improve the learning efficiency of routing strategies, the adaptive SHERB-MADDQN-based routing algorithm is designed.
In detail, the experience buffer of each agent is softly constructed
by embedding the state information of the destination BS in the reward.
Thus, the reward in (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In 3rd item ‣ III-A Dec-POMDP based Reformulation ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) is reformulated as</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)=\frac{1}{\mathcal{T}^{tr,t}_{u\kappa}(t)+\varsigma}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t)=\frac{1}{\mathcal{T}^{tr,t}_{u\kappa}(t)+\varsigma}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d_{u\kappa}(t)}{d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)}\eta_{u\kappa}^{r}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d_{u\kappa}(t)}{d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)}\eta_{u\kappa}^{r}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\in\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t),t\in T," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\in\mathcal{C}_{u}(t),\kappa\in\Gamma_{u}(t),t\in T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u\kappa}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u\kappa}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\kappa b}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\kappa b}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denote distances
from UAV <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to neighboring UAV <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, and from UAV <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> to destination BS <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ς</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter to balance the benefits from the delay and distance.
It is noted that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u\kappa}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u\kappa}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is positively related to the reward,
since a larger value of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u\kappa}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u\kappa}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a fewer hop counts required,
saving time in queuing for transmission.
Meanwhile, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the total transmission distance
from the selected next hop <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> to UAV <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and BS <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u\kappa}(t)+d_{\kappa b}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is closer to the straight shortest distance between UAV <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and BS <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>,
agent <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> may obtain the greater value of rewards, and vice versa.
Moreover, compared with the hard-HERB (HHERB)-based method that constructs
a hierarchical data structure to store the experience,
the SHERB can mitigate the problem of sparse experience samples,
improving the sample utilization efficiency and generalization ability of strategies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, when the dimensions of state and action spaces are large, it is tricky to maintain the Q-table in Q-learning.
Besides, the deep Q-network (DQN)-based algorithm may cause a large deviation
caused by overestimating the Q-target value.
Hence, by combining double Q-learning with DQNs, DDQN algorithms are proposed to approximate
Q-value functions via deep neural networks (DNNs) and decouple the action selection
and calculation of Q-target values <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>.
Further, for the DDQN, there exist two DNNs, i.e.,
the online network with parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>
and the target network with parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{-}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{-}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> of each agent <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Through constantly updating the weight <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> of online networks,
loss function <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> is trained and then minimized.
The experience replay buffer (ERB) of agent <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is designed to store the historical experience and denoted as
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}\!=\!\{(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}({t+1}),o_{u}({t+1}))|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}\!=\!\{(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}({t+1}),o_{u}({t+1}))|r\!\in\!\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By randomly sampling <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> transition tuples from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> is typically computed as the mean squared error between Q-value function
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t);\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t);\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> and Q-target <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> SHERB-MADDQN-based routing algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> .

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Optimal policy <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Pi^{*}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Pi^{*}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialization:</span> Initialize the network environment, hyper-parameters,
ERB set <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the online
and target network parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> for each agent <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each episode <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

 

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=1,\dots,U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=1,\dots,U</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
                 The observation of agent <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is set as <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
                 Allocate the bandwidth based on queued demands in <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> via (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In II-C Delay Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1,\dots,|\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1,\dots,|\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
                 Select action <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for demand <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> under observation <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
using an <math id="alg1.l8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy policy.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
                 Execute <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and obtain reward <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{D}_{u}|&gt;D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{D}_{u}|&gt;D</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

 

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
                 Randomly select <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> samples from <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
                  Compute Q-target value <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> via (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
                  Update <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> via the gradient descent in (<a href="#S3.E21" title="In III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
                  Periodically update target network parameter <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> via (<a href="#S3.E22" title="In III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) every <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> steps.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
                Update the environment,
and set observation <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)\leftarrow o_{u}({t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)\leftarrow o_{u}({t+1})</annotation></semantics></math> for all agents in <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
               Store transition <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1),o_{u}({t\!+\!1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1),o_{u}({t\!+\!1}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
of each demand <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> into corresponding <math id="alg1.l19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}L(\theta_{u})=\mathbb{E}_{\xi\thicksim\mathcal{D}_{u}}\left[\left(y_{u}(t)-Q(o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t);\theta_{u})\right)^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}L(\theta_{u})=\mathbb{E}_{\xi\thicksim\mathcal{D}_{u}}\left[\left(y_{u}(t)-Q(o_{u}(t),a_{u}(t);\theta_{u})\right)^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where tuple <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is a transition data of <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{u}(t)=\mathcal{R}_{u}({t+1})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{u}(t)=\mathcal{R}_{u}({t+1})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{u}Q(o_{u}({t+1}),\arg\max_{a^{\prime}_{u}(t)}Q(o_{u}({t+1}),a^{\prime}_{u}(t);\theta_{u}^{b})|\theta^{-}_{u})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{u}Q(o_{u}({t+1}),\arg\max_{a^{\prime}_{u}(t)}Q(o_{u}({t+1}),a^{\prime}_{u}(t);\theta_{u}^{b})|\theta^{-}_{u}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Besides, the gradient of <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{u}}L(\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{u}}L(\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is used to update <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> via the gradient descent, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}\theta_{u}\leftarrow\theta_{u}-\alpha_{u}\nabla_{\theta_{u}}L(\theta_{u})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}\theta_{u}\leftarrow\theta_{u}-\alpha_{u}\nabla_{\theta_{u}}L(\theta_{u}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Wherein, <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate that controls the size of update steps.
In every <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{-}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{-}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is periodically updated
to match the parameter of online network <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> for stabilizing training
and improving the convergence, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}\theta_{u}^{-}\leftarrow\tau\theta_{u}+(1-\tau)\theta_{u}^{-}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}\theta_{u}^{-}\leftarrow\tau\theta_{u}+(1-\tau)\theta_{u}^{-},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the soft update coefficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The detail of the proposed SHERB-MADDQN-based routing method is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Firstly, the algorithm initializes the network environment,
hyper-parameters, ERB set <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the parameters of DNNs, respectively (line <a href="#alg1.l1" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
At the beginning of each episode, the observation of agent <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized as <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (lines <a href="#alg1.l2" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l5" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
Then, according to (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In II-C Delay Model ‣ II System Model and Problem Formulation ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), the bandwidth of agent <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is allocated according to queued demands in <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l6" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Based on <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> selects sub-action <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for demand <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> via an <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy policy,
and then executes <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{u}^{r}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{u}^{r}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain reward <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}({t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}({t+1})</annotation></semantics></math> (lines <a href="#alg1.l7" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l10" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).
If the number of transition tuples in <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than mini-batch <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> samples are randomly selected to calculate
Q-target value <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> via (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) (lines <a href="#alg1.l11" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l13" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
Additionally, the DNN performs a gradient descent step to update <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l14" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
The target network parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{u}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{u}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> is periodically updated according to (<a href="#S3.E22" title="In III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>)
every <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> steps (line <a href="#alg1.l15" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
At time step <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, when all agents finish the actions of all demands, the environment is updated.
Further, each agent <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\!\in\!\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> obtains next observation <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}({t\!+\!1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}({t\!+\!1})</annotation></semantics></math> to update observation <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l18" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).
Besides, the transition <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1),o_{u}({t\!+\!1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o_{u}(t),a_{u}^{r}(t),\mathcal{R}_{u}^{r}(t\!+\!1),o_{u}({t\!+\!1}))</annotation></semantics></math>
of each demand <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is stored into corresponding <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> for training (line <a href="#alg1.l19" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B SHERB-MADDQN-based Routing Algorithm ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Simulation Results</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, a couple of simulations are conducted via Python.
Specifically, nodes of LAINs are distributed in the area within a 15km <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 5km range,
the altitude range of UAVs is within [0.2, 0.4]km.
UAVs are initialized by the ground control center at the beginning of missions.
Besides, the size of demands from SDs is randomly set within [400, 600]kbits.
Other parameters are set as: <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{min}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{min}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 10m, <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{u,max}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{u,max}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 100m,
<math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{ij}^{2}\!=\!-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mpadded style="width:0.608em;" width="0.608em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{ij}^{2}\!=\!-</annotation></semantics></math>110dBm, <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 2.4Ghz, <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\!=\!3\times 10^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\!=\!3\times 10^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>m/s, <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{tr}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{tr}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 40dBm,
<math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{max}_{i}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{max}_{i}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 50, <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{u}\!=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{u}\!=</annotation></semantics></math> 2MHz,
<math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varrho_{1}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varrho_{1}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 5.0188, <math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varrho_{2}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varrho_{2}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 0.3511,
<math id="S4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>LoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 0.1dB, and
<math id="S4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}\!=\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>LoS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{nm}^{\mathrm{LoS}}\!=\!</annotation></semantics></math> 21dB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22745v1/Rewards.svg" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/250;" width="333" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Comparisons of the four algorithms in terms of the accumulative reward during the training process.

</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22745v1/Loss.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/250;" width="333" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span>Comparisons of the four algorithms in terms of the convergence performance during the training process.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22745v1/Delay.svg" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/250;" width="333" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Comparisons of the four algorithms in terms of average E2E delay.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22745v1/Step.svg" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/250;" width="333" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>Comparisons of the four algorithms in terms of average hop counts.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the performance of Algorithm 1, different metrics are evaluated
by comparing with SHERB-MADQN, HHERB-MADDQN, and HHERB-MADQN algorithms in Figs. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>-<a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Specifically, in Fig. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the accumulative rewards are provided to evaluate the convergence performance.
It can be observed that all four algorithms converge with different performances.
In the first 2,000 episodes, rewards are not satisfactory.
As the number of episodes increases, rewards increase and converge at the specific values.
Besides, the rewards of SHERB-MADRL-based methods are larger compared to the rewards of HHERB-MADRL-based algorithms,
due to the higher learning efficiency of the proposed SHERB.
Meanwhile, the convergence value of the proposed SHERB-MADDQN algorithm is larger than the SHERB-MADQN algorithm.
Hence, according to the designed (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In 3rd item ‣ III-A Dec-POMDP based Reformulation ‣ III Problem Formulation and Algorithm Design ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) where rewards are negative, the proposed algorithm may have less delay for routing.
In Fig. <a href="#S4.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the loss functions of all four algorithms converge.
For the proposed SHERB-MADDQN, the convergence speed is faster and the curve fluctuation of loss functions has a narrower range.
Moreover, the loss value of the proposed method is smaller compared to other algorithms when the curve converges,
indicating a more stable and effective training process.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The E2E delay for transmitting demands is evaluated in Fig. <a href="#S4.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
It is observed that as demands grow, the E2E delay of the data transmission
increases for all algorithms, due to the limited resources of the bandwidth.
Nevertheless, the delay of the SHERB-MADDQN algorithm decreases by 24.09%, 20.49%, and 22.56%
than the delay of SHERB-MADQN, HHERB-MADDQN, and HHERB-MADQN algorithms, respectively.
Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ IV Simulation Results ‣ Trusted Routing for Blockchain-Enabled Low-Altitude Intelligent Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the performance of hop counts under different demand numbers.
Specifically, with the increasing demands, the average hop counts of all algorithms grow,
due to the increased congestion of networks.
Nevertheless, the SHERB-based algorithm requires fewer hop counts for transmitting demands,
benefiting from the better training performance of the algorithm.
In short, simulation results demonstrate that the proposed algorithm performs better during routing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusions</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we characterize the routing process of multiple sources and destinations in zero-trust LAINs, with the joining and exiting of UAVs.
Additionally, the blockchain technique is introduced to manage the mobility and verify identities,
enhancing the reliability and safety during routing.
Besides, the routing problem is formulated to minimize the total E2E delay with multi-constraints.
Further, we reformulate the routing problem into a Dec-POMDP to deal with the challenge of obtaining global information in LAINs
characterized by the high dynamic, distributed topology.
Then, to improve the learning efficiency of the MARL, a SHERB-MADDQN-based algorithm is proposed via
embedding the observed state into rewards.
Simulation results in LAINs demonstrate that the designed SHERB-MADDQN algorithm outperforms
in the delay, convergence, and loss value of training performances than other algorithms.</p>
</div>
</section>
